.SS Abstract
Provides a portable boolean interface for C that automatically adapts to
the compiler\(aqs native boolean implementation whenever available.
.PP
Rather than forcing a fixed type or value definitions,
\f[CR]BOOLEAN.H\f[R] detects the most suitable compiler\-supported
boolean type and constants, falling back to a portable implementation
only when necessary.
.PP
If a standard compiler boolean header (such as \f[CR]stdbool.h\f[R] or
an equivalent implementation) has already been included, this module
transparently adopts it.
.PP
Otherwise, it includes the appropriate compiler header itself before
exposing a consistent set of boolean definitions.
.PP
The result is a single, compiler\-independent interface that remains
fully compatible with existing code while preserving the compiler\(aqs
preferred boolean representation whenever possible.
